Looks like you ran out of good questions, and resorted to filler.
Here are a few better ones, if that was intended to be more than a
one-time joke:
 (minor vague spoilers)
Ever strip off your armor so a monster could attack you?
Ever been swallowed and escape?
Ever lie about your name to make a guard go away?
Ever cause an object to become embedded in a wall?
Ever been surrounded by stone and unable to move in any direction?
Ever search a level for an engraving?
Ever read the file of fortune cookie messages?
Ever do something ridiculous just because a fortune suggested it?
Ever write new rumors for fortune cookies? (Better than "Is your name Dave?")
Ever send yourself mail just to get a scroll of mail?
Ever manage to attack the mail daemon?
Ever meet the three stooges?
Ever destroy Vlad the Impaler?
Ever been about to die, and...
	... write an engraving to the person who finds your corpse/statue?
	... and given silly names to all the monsters in sight?
	... to all the objects in your inventory?
Ever quit when "already on Charon's boat"?
Ever die from a trip to heaven?
Ever die and come back as some monster other than a ghost?
Ever let a monster out of a bottle?
Ever had a potion explode on you?
Ever been hit in the face with a cream pie?
Ever train your pet to fetch?
Ever perform a human sacrifice?
Ever open a drawbridge?
Ever hear a monster insulting you?
Ever apply a tool to the edge of the screen?
Ever wonder where those shopkeeper names come from? (Ever find out?)
Ever quit or escape and start over to try to get a better starting inventory?

Enjoy life.  Play NetHack more often.
